  {
    "@id": "http://villainscope.org/villain/villain_movie_0107",
    "@type": [
      "http://villainscope.org/villain/Villain",
      "http://villainscope.org/villain/Character",
      "http://schema.org/Person",
      "http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/age": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
        "@value": 26
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "Music: Leitmotif. Symbolic Tune - Beckert incessantly whistles Edvard Grieg's \"In the Hall of the Mountain King\". This specific piece is symbolic, as it originally accompanied a scene where trolls sing about slaughtering the protagonist. The Trigger - The whistling functions as a nervous \"tic\" and a psychological \"trigger\" that awakens Beckert’s uncontrollable side shortly before he commits an atrocity. Evidence of Lack of Control -This musical leitmotif serves as a key piece of evidence that his personality is \"evenly bisected\" and that he cannot govern his own behavior, which ultimately leads the audience to take pity on him. | Sympathetic Villain: He is depicted as a man suffering from intense pain and anguish because he kills against his will. By portraying him as a pathetic victim of his own impulses, Lang forces the audience to feel empathy for a man who would normally be considered a monster. | Dual Personality: Reveal the \"torments of his soul\" and the internal struggle between his stable self and the \"demons\" that drive him to kill."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/gender": [
      {
        "@value": "Male"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/isPartOf": [
      {
        "@id": "http://villainscope.org/work/work_movie_0103"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Hans Beckert"
      }
    ],
    "http://villainscope.org/villain/appearsIn": [
      {
        "@id": "http://villainscope.org/work/work_movie_0103"
      }
    ],
    "http://villainscope.org/villain/distinctiveFeatures": [
      {
        "@value": "Hat"
      }
    ],
    "http://villainscope.org/villain/hasPersonalityTrait": [
      {
        "@id": "http://villainscope.org/trait/Brazenness"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://villainscope.org/trait/Chrisma"
